SDUSD::setDepositCap
├── when caller is not owner
│   └── it should revert with OwnableUnauthorizedAccount
└── when caller is owner
    ├── when new deposit cap equals the current cap
    │   └── it should revert with SDUSDNoStateChange
    └── when new deposit cap is different
        ├── it should update depositCap without changing depositCapUsage
        ├── it should emit DepositCapUpdated with the old and new cap
        ├── when new deposit cap is zero
        │   └── it should allow the update and disable new deposits and mints
        ├── when new deposit cap is below current usage
        │   ├── it should allow the update and disable new deposits and mints
        │   ├── it should not block withdrawals or redemptions
        │   └── withdrawals should reopen only the headroom created below the updated cap
        └── when new deposit cap is above current usage
            └── it should expose the difference as deposit headroom
